+      // reference, because an unassigned global throws ReferenceError
+      // where an undefined property is merely falsy. The inner try/catch
+      // covers the same ground the outer one does for the rest of the
+      // chain, but scoped: GTAOPass allocates two extra half-float render
+      // targets plus a depth texture and compiles two large shaders, so it
+      // is the likeliest construction here to fail on a real device, and a
+      // GTAO-only failure should cost GTAO only.
+      //
+      // POSITION: after RenderPass, before UnrealBloomPass, and that is
+      // three separate constraints all pointing the same way.
+      //   * Before OutputPass, because occlusion attenuates *light*. Its
+      //     Default output path multiplies the read buffer by the denoised
+      //     AO (GTAOBlendShader, CustomBlending DstColor x Zero), and a
+      //     multiply is only physically meaningful on linear radiance.
