+      //     GTAO's multiply belongs on linear ones. OutputPass's own class
+      //     doc only requires sRGB input for passes that need it; GTAO
+      //     does not -- it reads colour solely to scale it, and builds its
+      //     own depth/normal G-buffer from the scene, untouched by
+      //     whatever the colour buffer is encoded in.
+      //   * Before UnrealBloomPass, so bloom thresholds the darkened
+      //     image. Bloom after AO cannot bleed light back into a crease
+      //     the AO just closed; bloom before AO could, and the threshold
+      //     (1.8, fitted in plan 2 task 7) was fitted against the
+      //     pre-bloom linear buffer, which is what it still reads here.
+      //   * It renders its own scene depth+normal G-buffer (a full extra
+      //     scene pass with an override material), so it does not depend
